From: LilSmokeOS <dev@lilsmoke.local>
Subject: [PATCH] direct: pop the cleanup handler when joined during startup

direct_thread_main can return immediately after initialization if its creator
has already started joining it. That return bypasses pthread_cleanup_pop and
leaves musl's cancellation-cleanup chain pointing into the returned stack frame.
Use the common cleanup path for this case as well as a normal thread return.

Signed-off-by: LilSmokeOS <dev@lilsmoke.local>
---
 lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/thread.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/thread.c b/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/thread.c
--- a/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/thread.c
+++ b/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/thread.c
@@ -471,7 +471,8 @@ direct_thread_main( void *arg )
 
      if (thread->joining) {
           D_DEBUG_AT( Direct_Thread, "  -> Being joined before entering main routine!\n" );
-          return NULL;
+          ret = NULL;
+          goto cleanup;
      }
 
      D_MAGIC_ASSERT( thread, DirectThread );
@@ -488,6 +489,7 @@ direct_thread_main( void *arg )
 
      D_MAGIC_ASSERT( thread, DirectThread );
 
+cleanup:
      pthread_cleanup_pop( 1 );
 
      return ret;
